  "title": "The neural activity of auditory conscious perception: intracranial EEG epochs (Christison-Lagay et al. 2025; derivative: authors' 2-s grey-matter epochs)",
  "description": "This derivative dataset contains epoched, artifact-screened intracranial EEG (icEEG) recorded from adults with drug-resistant epilepsy who performed an auditory perceptual threshold task. A 75 ms target sound was embedded in white noise at each participant's 50% detection threshold. Trials are sorted into Perceived, Not Perceived and blank categories. The release holds 2-s epochs from grey-matter electrodes only, covering 30 participants and 32 recordings. The continuous recordings were not released.",
  "methods_description": "Subdural grid, strip and depth electrodes were recorded at Yale New Haven Hospital, Northwell Health and Mount Sinai. Participants reported whether they heard a sound and which one it was. The authors sorted trials by behaviour and removed epochs containing epileptic events by visual inspection. They then applied four-stage artifact rejection and kept only grey-matter electrodes. The epochs were repackaged into BrainVision float32 format with BIDS events and electrode metadata.",
